---
import SimpleContentLayout from "@/layouts/SimpleContentLayout.astro";
import { company } from "@/data/company";

// Mirror of legal/privacidad.astro (structure per art. 13 of Colombian Decree
// 1377 of 2013). Keep both versions in sync — see CLAUDE.md point 27.
const effectiveDate = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-US", {
  dateStyle: "long",
  timeZone: "UTC",
}).format(new Date(company.privacyPolicyEffectiveDate));
// Missing legal data in src/data/company.ts: the page shows in parentheses what
// must go there, so the gap stays visible until it is filled — see CLAUDE.md
// point 27.
const pending = {
  legalName: "(Exact legal name, as registered in the RUT or Chamber of Commerce certificate)",
  nit: "(Company tax ID with check digit, e.g. 901.234.567-8)",
  city: "(City and department of the main domicile, e.g. Cúcuta, Norte de Santander)",
  address: "(Company's physical address for notices)",
  phone: "(Company contact phone number, with country code, e.g. +57 300 000 0000)",
};
const domicile = `${company.city || pending.city}, ${company.country.en}`;
---

<SimpleContentLayout
  eyebrow="Legal"
  title="Privacy policy"
  intro="How Siscodex collects, uses and protects the information of people who visit this site or write to us through the contact form."
  description="Siscodex privacy and personal data processing policy, under Colombian Law 1581 of 2012."
  path="/en/legal/privacidad"
>
  <p>Effective as of {effectiveDate}.</p>

  {/*
    SECTION DISABLED ON PURPOSE: Siscodex is not legally incorporated yet, so there
    is no legal name, tax ID or domicile to publish (CLAUDE.md point 29). Once it is:
    fill src/data/company.ts, remove this comment (here and in legal/privacidad.astro)
    and renumber the sections starting from 1 = "Data controller" (+1 to all, and
    "See section 7" → 8).
  <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Legal name:</strong> {company.legalName || pending.legalName}</li>
    <li><strong>Tax ID (NIT):</strong> {company.nit || pending.nit}</li>
    <li><strong>Domicile:</strong> {domicile}</li>
    <li><strong>Address:</strong> {company.address || pending.address}</li>
    <li><strong>Phone:</strong> {company.phone || pending.phone}</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email for personal data matters:</strong>
      <a href={`mailto:${company.privacyEmail}`}>{company.privacyEmail}</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  */}
  <p>
    This policy is issued in compliance with Colombian Law 1581 of 2012, Decree 1377 of 2013
    (compiled in Decree 1074 of 2015) and other Colombian personal data protection regulations.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Data we collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Data you provide in the contact form:</strong> name, company, email, phone, service of interest
    and your project description.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Data generated automatically when you submit the form:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Approximate location</strong> (city, region and country), derived from your IP address by
      our infrastructure provider, Cloudflare. It is not your exact location: we do not use GPS or ask
      your browser for location permission, and it may be inaccurate if you use a VPN, a corporate network
      or mobile data.
    </li>
    <li>The date and time of submission and the site language you wrote from.</li>
    <li>
      Your IP address and technical browser signals, used by <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong> to
      verify that the submission comes from a person and not an automated program. Siscodex does not store
      your IP address.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Data generated while browsing the site:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong>, <strong>only if you accept cookies</strong> in the notice shown
      when you enter the site: it measures, in aggregate, how the site is used (pages visited, visit duration,
      device type, approximate country or city). See section 7.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your theme preference (light/dark) and your cookie choice are stored only in your own browser
      (local storage) and are not sent to any server.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not request sensitive data (health, racial or ethnic origin, political, religious or
    sexual orientation, biometric data, among others) or data from minors. Please do not include it
    in the form message.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Purposes of processing</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Responding to your contact request and following up on it.</li>
    <li>
      If you decide to move forward with a project, the commercial, contractual and technical
      management of the relationship with your organization.
    </li>
    <li>
      Using your approximate location to put the request in context (time zone, language and
      geographic coverage of our service).
    </li>
    <li>Protecting the form against spam, abuse and automated submissions.</li>
    <li>Producing aggregate site usage statistics to improve it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your data or share it with third parties for advertising purposes.</p>

  <h2>3. Authorization</h2>
  <p>
    By checking the authorization box and submitting the contact form, you grant your prior, express
    and informed authorization for the processing of your data under this policy. We keep a record
    of that authorization (date, time and submitted data) as proof, as required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Data processors and international transfers</h2>
  <p>
    To operate the site and the form, some providers process data on behalf of Siscodex, solely to
    provide their service to us:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> (United States): site hosting, anti-spam verification (Turnstile)
      and approximate IP geolocation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Resend</strong> (United States): delivery of the email that notifies us of your request.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Zoho Corporation</strong>: corporate mailbox where we receive and answer your request.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Google LLC</strong> (United States): site analytics (Google Analytics 4).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This means your data may be stored or processed outside Colombia. These transfers are made to
    providers that offer security and confidentiality guarantees, to countries that Colombia's
    Superintendence of Industry and Commerce considers to have an adequate level of data protection,
    or under each provider's contractual safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your rights as a data subject</h2>
  <p>Under article 8 of Law 1581 of 2012, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Know, update and correct your personal data.</li>
    <li>Request proof of the authorization you granted.</li>
    <li>Be informed about how your data has been used.</li>
    <li>
      Revoke the authorization and/or request deletion of your data when there is no legal or
      contractual duty to keep it.
    </li>
    <li>Access your personal data free of charge.</li>
    <li>
      File complaints with the Superintendence of Industry and Commerce (SIC), after completing the
      inquiry or claim process with Siscodex.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. How to exercise your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Write to <a href={`mailto:${company.privacyEmail}`}>{company.privacyEmail}</a>, including your
    full name, the email or phone number you contacted us with, and your request. Our data subject
    support team responds:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Inquiries</strong> (what data we hold and how we use it): within 10 business days of receipt,
      extendable by 5 more business days, with notice of the reason.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Claims</strong> (correction, update, deletion or revocation): within 15 business days, extendable
      by 8 more business days, with notice of the reason. The claim must include your identification,
      a description of the facts, your contact address and any supporting documents. If it is incomplete,
      we will ask you to complete it within the following 5 days.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cookies">7. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses Google Analytics 4, which sets Google first-party cookies (for example,
    <code>_ga</code>) to tell visits apart and produce aggregate statistics. We do not use
    advertising cookies.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>They are only enabled with your consent.</strong> When you enter the site we ask whether
      you accept them; until you do, Google Analytics is not loaded and no data is sent to Google. Rejecting
      them does not affect the site or the contact form.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You can change your mind at any time</strong> from the "Cookie preferences" link at the
      bottom of every page. If you withdraw consent, we stop sending data and delete the Google Analytics
      cookies from your browser.
    </li>
    <li>
      Your choice is remembered for 12 months; after that we ask again. You can also block or delete
      cookies in your browser settings.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Retention and security</h2>
  <p>
    We keep your data for as long as needed to handle your request and, if a business relationship
    arises, for as long as it lasts and for the period required by legal, accounting or contractual
    obligations. It is deleted afterwards. The site uses an encrypted connection (HTTPS), and access
    to received requests is restricted to the Siscodex team that handles them.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we substantially change this policy, we will publish the new version on this page with its
    updated effective date.
  </p>
</SimpleContentLayout>
